# ShortDescription is the line shown in `winget search`. The platform constraint goes
# first, because that is the one fact that decides whether the tool can work at all.
ShortDescription: Windows-only PowerPoint automation CLI - requires Microsoft PowerPoint to be installed.

Description: |-
  pptcli automates Microsoft PowerPoint from the command line through PowerPoint's
  native COM API: create and edit slides, shapes, text, tables, charts, images,
  animations and transitions, apply themes, run VBA macros, and export to PDF, images
  or video.

  REQUIREMENTS - read before installing:
  - Windows only. The tool drives PowerPoint through COM interop, which does not exist
    on macOS or Linux. There is no cross-platform build and there cannot be one.
  - Microsoft PowerPoint 2016 or later must be installed on the same machine. This
    package does not include PowerPoint and cannot work without it.
  - A desktop session. pptcli controls a real PowerPoint process, so it is not suitable
    for headless or server-side batch processing.
  - The .NET 9 Desktop Runtime, installed automatically as a dependency.

  The same functionality is also available as an MCP server for AI assistants; see the
  project page.

